WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.934
The Florida governor is

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.868
making waves

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.869
even before he's

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:03.770
expected to jump

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.405
into the presidential race.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:08.274
DeSantis today signed a bill to defund

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.610
diversity programs at Florida colleges,

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:11.745
a clear response

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:12.946
to critical race theory

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.814
being taught in classrooms.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.549
He's also changing

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:17.250
Florida law

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.452
to allow himself to campaign

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:20.520
while serving as governor

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.990
and to reduce transparency over his state

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.425
spending and travel.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.793
DeSantis is also stepping

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.495
in to ward off of his turf,

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.629
sending migrants

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:30.497
who come to Florida

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.432
to states run by Democrats

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.101
and wading into a New York City case

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.102
praising the Marine

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:36.903
veteran

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.838
now charged in the subway

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.140
chokehold death.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.809
He also barnstormed the trail in Iowa

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:43.643
this weekend

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:44.878
when the 45th president

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.846
canceled a rally there over

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.081
whether concerns

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.649
Donald Trump is taking notice

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.551
and taking aim at DeSantis.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:55.021
And DeSantis is indirectly firing back.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.857
We must reject

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.559
the culture of losing

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.127
that has infected our party

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:01.995
in recent years.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:04.297
If we focus the election on the past

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.299
or on other side issues,

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.500
then I think the Democrats

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.803
are going to beat us again.

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.604
Trump was asked for his response

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.640
in a new interview and declared, quote,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.542
I'm not at all caught up in the past.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.543
And second of all,

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:18.378
I'm doing much better against Biden

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.879
than he has in the polls.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:20.947
And third of all,

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.715
I did very well in the midterms.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.017
Ron's not a winner

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.919
because Ron without me

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.787
wouldn't have won today.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:28.855
DeSantis was asked

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.324
Do you think Trump lost in 20?

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.092
20?

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.893
This was his answer.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:35.662
Look at the last

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.198
however many election cycles. 20, 18.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.933
We lost the House.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.501
We lost the Senate.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.802
20, 20.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.504
Biden becomes president. Ergo.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:44.904
Excuse me.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.873
We lost the Senate in 20, 20.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.541
Biden becomes president.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.910
And it's done a huge amount of damage.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.379
Very unpopular in 20, 22.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:54.481
And we are supposed

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.982
to have this big red wave.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.118
And other than like Florida and Iowa.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.319
I didn't see a red wave

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.386
across this country.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.289
And so I think the party has developed

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:04.858
a culture of losing

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.062
Joining me now is former Trump

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.230
adviser Steve Cortez.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:10.530
Thank you

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.333
so much for joining the program, Steve.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.034
Sarah, thank you for having me.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:15.768
All right.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:19.172
So, Steve, you were a staunch, unwavering

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.407
supporter of Donald Trump

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.408
during the presidency

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.210
and even before he was president.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.647
Why are you backing Ron DeSantis now

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.950
instead of Donald Trump?

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.920
Sarah, listen, I was honored to advocate

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.888
for President Trump

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.089
and for the America

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:38.158
First Movement broadly for many years.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.260
I now believe that this is the next

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.829
natural phase of that movement.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.396
And by that

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.130
I mean that

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.865
I believe that Governor DeSantis

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.367
is the most electable,

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.035
most conservative candidate

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.937
out there who can both win

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.205
the general election,

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.707
as well as govern effectively,

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.376
as actually implement

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.944
through discipline and focus

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:59.612
the most conservative policy

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:00.647
agenda possible

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:01.614
I believe he has proven that

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.750
by his track record in Florida.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.218
And for that reason, I'm

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:07.220
taking the personal risk here

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:07.987
of advocating

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:08.988
for the underdog,

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:11.090
for the political renegade the outsider

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.592
who is Ron DeSantis.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.826
So I have to ask you,

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:14.160
Governor

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.262
DeSantis has not actually announced

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.364
he's actually running for president.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.400
So I guess the question is,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.568
do you know something we don't know?

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.669
I mean, has he told you?

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.537
Yes, I am planning to do this

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.206
or giving you any indication that, yeah,

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:26.906
he's going to run

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.475
Well, Sarah, it's

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:29.776
not my

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.711
place to talk about private conversations

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.512
with Governor DeSantis.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:34.214
I will let him make that announcement

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.215
at the appropriate time.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.583
But I think any

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:39.285
but I think any any reasonable observer

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.588
will conclude that Ron DeSantis is doing

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.389
everything that a person does

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.225
to prepare to make this run for office.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.593
So I fully expect that

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.894
that is forthcoming

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.562
in the coming days and weeks.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.863
And I personally very,

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.532
very excited about it because, again,

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:53.666
I believe that, look,

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.268
the country is in a very miserable mood

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:55.668
right now.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.170
And that's not Steve Cortez's opinion.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.304
That's what all of the relevant

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.572
polling shows us.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.673
For example, 70%

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.542
of the American people in a Fox News poll

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.477
say that the economy is getting worse

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.845
for this for their family.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.981
So we are in a very depressed state

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.315
in the country right now.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.017
It will not help the country psyche.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:11.784
It will not help the country

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:12.885
from a policy standpoint

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.188
to have a rematch of the 20, 20 election

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.856
that almost no one wants.

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.458
We've seen this movie before.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:19.926
Biden versus Trump.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:20.860
No one likes it.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.095
We know the ending.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.896
And polling reflects that again.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:24.764
AP polling.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.899
70% of the American people say

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.534
they do not want President

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.569
Trump to run again.

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:30.336
Same numbers.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.038
70% of the people in NBC

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:32.472
polling say

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.440
they do not want Joe Biden to run again.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.908
So how do we prevent that rematch?

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.910
How do we break this political logjam?

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.178
So that we can start to resurrect

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.680
the American spirit?

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.382
I believe that the most credible way

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.016
the solution,

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:43.983
the antidote

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.418
is Governor Ron DeSantis,

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.453
this political rising star,

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.322
this young man of dynamism

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:49.856
who took

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:51.391
what was a swing state

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:53.493
and turned it into a ruby red

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.527
Republican state.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:55.862
You said that you

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.497
endorsed Donald Trump partly

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:58.831
because he was a disruptor.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:01.668
And you think DeSantis is the same thing.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.136
I'm curious what you

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.070
you meant by that,

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.071
because Donald Trump

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.739
certainly was a disruptor,

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.207
but he did not follow

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.742
some of the norms of the president.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.944
You see from historical past.

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.613
He was a liar.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:14.647
He lied a lot.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.516
He was a president who stoked division

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.318
and anger and Trump denies this.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:18.751
But there are

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.753
some people who were convicted

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:22.221
of seditious conspiracy

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.157
who said they blamed Donald Trump

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.625
for their actions

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:27.360
breaking into the Capitol

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.395
Would you be okay

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.230
if DeSantis acted in the same

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.266
way as former President Trump

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:35.768
Well, Sarah, you and I

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.036
are certainly not going to agree.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.071
I do not think

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.539
that Donald Trump is a liar.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.274
I think he was exactly the disrupter

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:43.509
that we needed. Well, he has this time.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.511
But just because he realizes to be fair,

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.480
he has been caught lying. Okay.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.548
Over and over and over again.

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:49.782
Let's be fair.

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:50.850
I mean, I care about that.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.217
I'm here

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:51.751
to advocate

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:52.652
for Governor DeSantis,

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:53.886
but give me a Trump lie

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.054
then, and let's discuss it.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.222
There are too many of them

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:57.323
to even recount,

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:59.659
literally too many to recount.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:01.060
But I will I will do this.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.962
Let us talk about DeSantis then.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.030
The Republican Party

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.198
has been best known

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.500
for wanting a smaller government,

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:10.737
a party that wants fiscal responsibility.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.406
A historically has been pro-business.

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:14.040
And I'm curious

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.007
what you think

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:17.410
about something that he has done,

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.978
which is basically wanting

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:21.047
to put a bill in place,

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:22.115
wanting to put a law in place

00:06:22.115 --> 00:06:23.349
that doesn't allow people

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:24.117
to look

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:25.718
at his past record

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.653
and some of the way he spent money

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:28.921
and some of the state

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.223
using some of the state

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:33.359
resources like the airplane

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:34.360
doesn't want people to be able

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.095
to look at that and be transparent

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:38.464
about what his history was

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:39.832
as the governor of Florida.

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:42.935
What do you think about that as a law?

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:43.536
Sure.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:44.137
Well, Sara,

00:06:44.137 --> 00:06:45.805
to the first part of your question,

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:46.005
you know,

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.140
regarding his willingness

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.908
to take on big business. Yes.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:50.977
Historically, the Republican Party

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:53.146
was very much allied with big business,

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:54.881
but that is not the new Republican Party.

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:56.249
That is not the patriotic

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:58.117
populist movement, which is pro-worker,

00:06:58.117 --> 00:06:59.752
which is pro small business.

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:00.153
And so Ron

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.421
DeSantis has shown

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:02.822
an incredible amount of courage

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:05.024
in taking on the oligarchs

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.692
and their power, particularly Disney,

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:08.761
the most powerful company in his state,

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.329
who tried to insert itself

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:12.498
into a cultural political question

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:14.066
about whether or not it's appropriate

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:16.002
to teach sexualized content

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:17.236
to extremely young children.

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.271
The people of Florida

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:19.906
made their decision that it is not.

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:21.908
And that is not good education

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:23.276
for very young children.

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:24.644
And Disney tried to flex

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:26.078
its corporate muscle

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:26.712
and impose

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:29.015
its will on the people of Florida.

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:30.450
Ron DeSantis has punched back

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.384
very hard at Disney

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:33.453
and other giant corporations now

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:35.087
to the second part of your question

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:36.722
regarding his travels, as you know.

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.357
Let me once somebody becomes a governor,

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:40.359
I just want to jump in about Disney.

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:41.327
But I guess the question is,

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:42.962
since Republicans for such a long time

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:44.430
were very much pro-business,

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.899
wanted businesses to be able to operate

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:48.134
the way they saw fit

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:50.336
and let the let the public decide, do

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:53.072
you do you agree that that is a different

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:55.575
in how the Republicans used to think

00:07:57.777 --> 00:07:58.444
I think there is.

00:07:58.444 --> 00:07:59.178
Yes, there is.

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:00.513
I will certainly agree

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:01.948
that the Republican Party of today

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:04.484
is far more populist, far more pro-worker

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:06.719
than it was in the past.

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:07.920
But here's the reality.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.255
Big business in this country

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:10.923
in many ways has been fuzed

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:12.792
with government power, particularly

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:13.893
if we look at big tech.

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.628
But there are many other areas as well

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:17.697
where big business and big government

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:19.632
work in concert with each other.

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:20.533
And I believe

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:22.268
that's why this country in many ways

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:23.503
has really slouched

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:26.105
into oligarchy, into the rule of the few.

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:27.807
We have a very different vision

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:29.308
of diffused power

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:31.110
of the people actually ruling.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.278
And part of that means

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:33.846
being willing to take on big business.

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:35.715
So I guess the term I would use to is

00:08:35.715 --> 00:08:37.316
we are pro enterprise

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:38.017
we're not pro

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:40.186
big business, we are pro free enterprise.

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:41.487
And it by the way, enterprise

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:43.155
has absolutely flourished

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:44.490
in the state of Florida

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.359
because people and businesses

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:49.028
are flocking in absolute record numbers

00:08:49.195 --> 00:08:49.862
to Florida

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:51.130
because of what Ron

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.365
DeSantis has done there,

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:53.432
because of what he has built.

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:54.467
So corporate media

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:55.601
wants to try to pretend

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:56.702
that Florida has become

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:58.771
some sort of unwelcoming backwater.

00:08:58.871 --> 00:09:01.107
But the actual reality of domestic

00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:03.342
migration of moving trucks and companies

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:05.578
pouring into the Sunshine State

00:09:05.578 --> 00:09:07.313
tells us exactly the opposite.

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:07.547
All right.

00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:08.014
Let's quick

00:09:08.014 --> 00:09:10.850
rallied to the decision to go to the

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:12.285
the other issue that we talked about,

00:09:12.285 --> 00:09:13.219
which is transparency.

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:13.920
And conservatives

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.154
have typically been champions

00:09:15.154 --> 00:09:16.822
of transparent

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:18.457
and more transparency in government.

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:20.159
But DeSantis in court cases

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:22.094
has lately claimed executive privilege.

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:22.562
And again,

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:24.196
we talked about that bill

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:25.598
that would exempt records

00:09:25.598 --> 00:09:26.999
related to his travel

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:28.000
from the state's

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.002
robust public disclosure law.

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:31.904
We do have the sunshine laws in Florida.

00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:32.972
What do you make of this?

00:09:32.972 --> 00:09:34.740
Do you agree that he should

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.975
be in this position to say,

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:36.642
hey, you can't

00:09:36.642 --> 00:09:38.244
you can't see the way

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:39.845
I've spent some of the state's money,

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:41.213
the taxpayer dollars,

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:44.216
or you can't have any of his staff

00:09:44.417 --> 00:09:47.320
testify claiming executive privilege.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.187
What do you make of that?

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:50.556
Well, saying

00:09:50.556 --> 00:09:51.057
listen, I think

00:09:51.057 --> 00:09:51.757
executive privilege

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:53.392
is very important for a president,

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:55.194
very important certainly for a governor.

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:55.561
As you

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:57.029
well know, a governor can't travel

00:09:57.029 --> 00:09:58.397
the way you and I can

00:09:58.397 --> 00:09:59.465
because of security measures.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:00.199
So he has to travel

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:01.400
in a very different way.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:02.101
Now,

00:10:02.602 --> 00:10:04.236
assuming that he does have to make

00:10:04.236 --> 00:10:04.804
his investors

00:10:04.804 --> 00:10:06.272
have to travel in a different way

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:08.074
and they don't use executive privilege,

00:10:08.074 --> 00:10:09.342
that is usually

00:10:09.342 --> 00:10:10.142
set aside

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:11.644
for presidents and presidents do

00:10:11.644 --> 00:10:13.279
use it at times.

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:15.047
So why is he special?

00:10:15.047 --> 00:10:16.983
Listen, I think that governor

00:10:16.983 --> 00:10:17.883
Governor DeSantis

00:10:17.883 --> 00:10:19.719
has been incredibly transparent.

00:10:19.719 --> 00:10:20.586
It's one of the reasons,

00:10:20.586 --> 00:10:21.621
one of the many reasons

00:10:21.621 --> 00:10:22.688
why Floridians

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:24.523
so rallied to his cause

00:10:24.523 --> 00:10:25.591
and gave him an absolutely

00:10:25.591 --> 00:10:27.193
overwhelming reelection.

00:10:27.193 --> 00:10:27.693
And, by the way,

00:10:27.693 --> 00:10:28.561
one with coattails,

00:10:28.561 --> 00:10:29.295
not just it's

00:10:29.295 --> 00:10:30.997
not just that he soared to it

00:10:30.997 --> 00:10:31.731
to a runaway

00:10:31.731 --> 00:10:33.399
smashing landslide victory,

00:10:33.399 --> 00:10:34.233
but he also lifted

00:10:34.233 --> 00:10:35.801
all other Florida statewide

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:37.103
officeholders the first time

00:10:37.103 --> 00:10:38.437
that all of those offices are held

00:10:38.437 --> 00:10:39.105
by Republicans

00:10:39.105 --> 00:10:39.572
the first time

00:10:39.572 --> 00:10:40.906
since the Civil War

00:10:40.906 --> 00:10:42.608
era in the Sunshine State.

00:10:42.608 --> 00:10:44.844
So the people of Florida clearly

00:10:44.844 --> 00:10:46.412
are more than satisfied with the job

00:10:46.412 --> 00:10:47.413
he is doing with the level

00:10:47.413 --> 00:10:49.215
of transparency that he's providing.

00:10:49.215 --> 00:10:50.182
And I believe he will continue

00:10:50.182 --> 00:10:51.017
to provide that

00:10:51.017 --> 00:10:52.385
as long as he's governor of Florida,

00:10:52.385 --> 00:10:53.819
until he becomes president.

00:10:53.819 --> 00:10:54.420
The United States,

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.788
which I hope to be a big part

00:10:55.788 --> 00:10:56.522
of making happen.

